2026-07-30 — PARTIAL audit only. The SHA above is deliberately NOT bumped.
[merge note: this section was written when the marker above read ef4c19a;
 main has since moved it to d73b1d6. "The SHA above" below means ef4c19a.]

Scope actually covered: the #459-follow-on commit (route/preview/undo for a
placement block) and nothing else. 34 commits now sit between ef4c19a and
HEAD; they were NOT audited, so bumping the SHA would record "parity
confirmed" for a span nobody checked.

Gap FOUND AND FIXED in that commit (the Class-2 shape CLAUDE.md warns about):
  --group / --preview / --undo all fell through manifest_to_plan into the
  generic `params` bucket, where ai_plan drops any param with no matching
  dialog control — and `nets` then defaults to ['*']. A recorded
      route.py in.kicad_pcb out.kicad_pcb --undo --group decap:U3
  converted to a plan step that ROUTES the whole board: the inverse operation
  at ~100x the scope, silently. --group/--group-scope/--group-by are now
  hoisted to the step (like --component) and resolved by
  ai_plan._group_net_names; --undo/--preview/--list-groups are refused with a
  loud per-command stderr warning. Two gates added, both verified to FAIL when
  the fix is reverted rather than merely to pass:
  test_manifest_plan_parity.check_group_flags (no wx) and
  tests/gui_parity/test_group_scope_parity.py (re-execs into KiCad python;
  CLI vs GUI internal 14=14, touching 20=20).

FOUND AND FIXED (was recorded here as open; the attribution below it was
wrong and is corrected):
  test_gui_engine_parity copper sets had gone from IDENTICAL at ef4c19a to
  segments CLI=1307 / GUI=1308, the delta being 58 GND plane taps on F.Cu at
  IDENTICAL coordinates with DIFFERENT width -- CLI 0.127, GUI 0.3. VERDICT
  still printed "PARITY" because the graded metrics (DRC, kicad unconnected)
  did not move; only the copper-set comparison saw it.

  Root cause is ONE line, and it is not a routing change at all:
      swig_gui.reset_params_to_defaults():  self.impedance_value.SetValue(50.0)
  impedance_value is a wx.SpinCtrl (INTEGER); on wxPython 4.2 a float raises
  TypeError. ai_plan's per-step reset CATCHES that and logs "per-step reset
  skipped", so the reset ABANDONED ITSELF at that line -- and the #439 loop
  that un-checks every geometry-floor override box sits ~80 lines BELOW it.
  With those boxes left checked from an earlier step, _effective_geometry_floor
  returned the just-reset routing_defaults value instead of the board's Default
  net-class. Plan step 1 passes track_width 0.127; step 2 (route_planes) omits
  it, meaning "use the board's" -- and got 0.3.

  The design and the #439 un-check loop were both already CORRECT. Nothing
  needed adding: a first attempt here added a second un-check loop and was
  removed as redundant duplication once the real cause was found. The fix is
  SetValue(defaults.IMPEDANCE_DEFAULT). After it: segments 1307=1307, vias
  144=144, cli-only 0, gui-only 0, copper sets IDENTICAL.

  Why this marker recorded IDENTICAL at ef4c19a while the same code diverged
  here: the defect predates the marker (reset_params_to_defaults and the
  hardcoded 50.0 both arrived in e8c72fe, an ANCESTOR of ef4c19a), so it is
  not a regression in the 34-commit span. It is wxPython-build dependent --
  older builds coerced a float into SpinCtrl.SetValue silently, this one
  (wxPython 4.2.2 / wx 3.3.2, Windows) raises. The earlier suspicion recorded
  here that d9bccbd ("power TRACES get ampacity") caused it was WRONG; no
  bisect is needed.

  Regression gate: tests/gui_parity/test_geometry_floor_leak.py, which asserts
  the OBSERVABLE resolved floors rather than trusting that the reset ran --
  a caught-and-logged exception in a reset is otherwise indistinguishable from
  a reset that worked. Verified to fail (exit 1) with the fix reverted.

